PRETABLE ADDENDUM -- #562 armmsrmodekill -- the `latch ind` row (written 2026-10-07 after table 1, before table 2b)

WHY: table 1's M_shared_msrpop scored 25/25 (an ESCAPE).  cpu_arm.h's #562 comment CLAIMS the three guest declines and
the two backstops "each announce once per CPU, independently" (claim -> row), and no row fired two declines in one
process, so a shared latch bit was invisible.  L1 (pre-ship construction): the row was added in-round.

ROW `latch ind`: one session fires all three guest declines -- MSR CPSR_c,#0x14 (msr_imm), MSR SPSR_c,#0x14 then
LDM {..pc}^ (arm_pop), and the target's MOVS pc,lr restoring the same SPSR (dpi S-to-pc).
  want  m=13 if=0 sp msr pop dpi   (one tag per site, each matched by its FUNCTION NAME; no Save/Load backstop text)
  kills M_shared_msrpop, M_shared_msrdpi, M_shared_popdpi, M_shared_latch
  channel: the per-site announce text -- a shared bit suppresses the second site's message, so its tag goes missing.
  Measured (killtable2): msrpop 25/26 (pop text missing), msrdpi 25/26 (dpi missing), popdpi 25/26 (dpi missing).

First version was UNSATISFIABLE (want lacked the classifier's `once` token; fixed build 25/26) -- caught by the main
loop reading FIXED_probe2.out before the mutants ran; the aborted run is labelled in KILLTABLE.out.
DISCLOSED, NOT ROWED: a decline bit shared with a BACKSTOP bit (no row fires a decline and a backstop in one process).
